# Line endings, for the one case where they are load-bearing.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout for anything it decides is text. A shell script survives that
# badly: the shebang becomes `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, the CR is taken as part
# of the interpreter's name, and Git Bash or WSL answers
# `bash\r: No such file or directory`. Every entry point this project has is
# a shell script, so the checkout would arrive unusable.
#
# These files hold LF on every platform. Everything else is left to Git's own
# judgement, which is right for it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The OpenDRIVE maps are handed to CARLA's parser as one string. It has never
# been asked to read a CRLF map and there is no reason to be the first.
*.xodr text eol=lf
